# PART 15 – UNDERSTANDING STATIC PODS

A Static Pod is a Pod managed directly by the kubelet on a particular node. Unlike normal Pods, Static Pods are not created through the API Server in the usual way.
Kubeadm uses Static Pods to run the main Control Plane components.

Example:
/etc/kubernetes/manifests/

If we inspect:
sudo cat /etc/kubernetes/manifests/kube-apiserver.yaml
Now, we will find the configuration used to run the API Server.

## What happens if the API Server goes down?
The kubelet can continue managing the local Control Plane Static Pods, but normal API operations and cluster management will be disrupted. This demonstrates why the kubelet and Static Pods are important.

